      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your argument effectively centers on the concept of \"tipping points,\" where immediate, localized disruptions are negligible compared to the existential threat of irreversible climate collapse. You should highlight that the economic chaos is temporary and will be outweighed by the long-term costs of inaction, including extreme weather damage and lost productivity in shifting labor markets. Additionally, framing this as a moral imperative emphasizes that economic models must prioritize human survival and planetary stability over short-term market convenience. To strengthen your paper, consider citing historical precedents where delayed action led to catastrophic costs, proving that those very decisions are more dangerous than any necessary transition price spike.",
